      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-02-stop-ruining-it",
      "title": "Stop Ruining It",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://seths.blog/2026/06/stop-ruining-it/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48368059\nPoints: 182\n# Comments: 90",
      "body": "Paul McGowan makes stereos. To paraphrase his insight: The musicality isn’t a feature you add to an amplifier. It’s what’s left when you stop ruining it.\nTo expand: Customer delight isn’t something we add to our projects. It’s what’s left if we don’t ruin it.\nCuriosity isn’t simply what’s left after a complete education. It’s still there if the system doesn’t ruin it.\nOr perhaps: Satisfaction in our work isn’t created by the boss. It’s what’s left if they don’t ruin it.\nAnd one last one: Trust isn’t something a brand builds with an ad campaign. It’s what’s left if the marketers don’t ruin it.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "herbertl",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-02T09:52:42.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://seths.blog/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/seth_godin_ogimages_v02_1806138-1.jpg",
