ocked (20 tables, multi-tenant by lender_id, idempotent CSV imports, append-only event log). Wireframes in progress. Hiring one engineer for the full ~6-month build via a paid bake-off: $5k flat for ~1 week of work, 2-3 candidates in parallel, winner takes the engagement. Losing candidates get paid in full and keep their work.Trial scope: CSV loan tape import with idempotent upsert + audit, one case detail screen, one LLM call classifying a borrower email reply with structured output, activity log driven by case events. Stack is contractor's choice — Postgres required, Next.js + TS or Python + React expected.Looking for senior generalists with real production LLM experience (structured outputs, evals, failure modes — not side-project tier) and strong relational data modeling judgment. Opinions you'll defend in writing.Email: info@readifinancial.comwith: one paragraph on why this interests you, 1-2 links to shipped work involving a real schema + LLM in production, your rate and availability, and one question about the project. No cover letters.Search terms: postgres, multi-tenant, LLM, OpenAI, Anthropic, Next.js,TypeScript, Python, fintech, vertical SaaS, founding engineer, contract, Canada\nBeatdapp | Machine Learning (ML) Engineer | Vancouver, Canada | ONSITE (Hybrid) | Full-timeBeatdapp is a ~50-person startup delivering audio and streaming integrity technology to media platforms. We process data at TB/PB scale to protect the royalty ecosystem, generate authentic recommendations, and detect AI-generated content.We are looking for an experienced ML engineer (+3 years) to work on our inference systems and data platform. In this role, you will be executing ML engineering, cloud platform/infrastructure design, and building ML model inference systems. You'll be a good fit if you have deep experience across different data stores, distributed systems, caching, and data transfer protocols. Our team manages and maintains integrated software systems, including inference containers, data processing pipelines, and feature stores/generation platforms.Stack: Multi-cloud (AWS, GCP), Docker, Airflow, Python, MLflow, BigQuery, SQL, S3, GCS, GitHub Actions, Terraform.The team is collaborative, and low-ego - we're looking for talented engineers who are comfortable working on projects that move at the pace of weeks rather than months and who love learning. Nice-to-haves include experience with audio/media systems, signal processing/spectograms, speech detection systems, computer vision, GPU hardware development, and event streaming systems.Full posting: https://beatdapp.breezy.hr/p/fcefc290c7b0-ml-engineer-ii-inf...Or reach me directly: kevin [at] beatdapp.com\nJoin (join.build) | Staff Software Engineer (Web) | REMOTE (US & Canada) | Full-Time | $175K–$205K + equity | React/Go/PostgresJoin is SaaS for the construction industry — we bring contractors, owners, and design teams onto one platform to coordinate high-value projects.You'll work across our flagship collaboration app: shaping frontend architecture and UI quality, influencing engineering-wide standards, and shipping with urgency while weighing long-term tradeoffs. We're hiring across profiles — frontend-heavy, fullstack, and backend-heavy — and want someone T-shaped across React/Go/Postgres with deep expertise in at least one.Stack: React/TypeScript (Vite, RTL, Cypress), Go, Postgres, AWS, Terraform.You: senior/staff-level experience; strong in at least one of React, Go, or Postgres; a clear communicator who mentors and reviews well.Apply: email jon@join.build with your resume, whether you lean frontend or backend, and — if you can — a PR review you've given that had a positive impact. Mention HN.\nTrashLab | Product, Eng | Full-time SF HybridWe are building the agentic operating system for waste collection and processing companies across the US.Join our team as a product manager or product engineer and own products end-to-end, working alongside a fully AI native team.Apply at our careers page or email john@trashlab.io with a resume and the most impactful codex/claude code skill you've developed or used.https://trashlab.com/careers\nRelevant Healthcare | Software Engineers (multiple levels) | Remote (US/Canada) | Full-timeRelevant builds a data platform that helps safety-net healthcare providers deliver better care using data from their electronic health records. Our customers are non-profit clinics called Community Health Centers. You can read more about them, us, and the roles on our jobs page: https://relevant.healthcare/jobs/We're a small team (~25 overall). We're bootstrapped (no external capital whatsoever, VC or otherwise) and profitable. We've got a modern tech stack (Rails, Typescript, React, GraphQL, d3) and a healthy approach to both tech debt and work/life balance… and we’re also a very nice group of people that get to work on interesting problems for some of the few unimpeachably good actors in healthcare!\nLove the focus on ethics for this job post, hopefully you can find my resume in the sea of emails, this role sounds very exciting!\nSmarterDx | 150-250k+ + equity + benefits | Remote (US only) | Multiple roles | https://smarterdx.com/careersSmarterDx builds clinical AI for one of healthcare’s most broken systems: how hospitals get paid for the care they actually deliver.Our physician-designed clinical AI platform reviews the clinical record, understands the nuance of patient care, and helps hospitals capture appropriate reimbursement across the revenue cycle. The core problem is hard: messy clinical data, complex regulations, payer rules, medical reasoning, and real financial stakes. When we get it right, hospitals recover millions in earned revenue, reduce manual review burden, and keep clinical and revenue teams focused on higher-value work.We’ve hit serious scale while keeping the team unusually strong and technical: MD/data scientist hybrids, Stanford LLM researchers, former Google and Amazon engineers, former ASF board member, and others who are among the best in their fields. Many teammates have been here since we bootstrapped to $1M+ in contracted revenue before raising capital.In 2025, SmarterDx became part of Smarter Technologies through a $1.1B deal with New Mountain Capital, reaching unicorn status while continuing to operate with the autonomy, urgency, and product velocity that got us here. Before that, we raised $71M from Floodgate, Transformation Capital, and Bessemer, including a $50M Series B.We have real product-market fit: 85+ health systems, 300+ hospital sites, rapid customer growth, and 150% YoY headcount growth (currently at ~500). Now we’re scaling the platform.For more and to apply, see https://smarterdx.com/careers\nClose | 100% REMOTE (US only) | Full Time | Bootstrapped & Profitable- Software Engineer (Backend)\n- Software Engineer Support (internal team)Close is hiring four engineers — Sr. Backend Engineer (Python), Sr. Frontend Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer, and a Software Engineer for our Support team (internal tooling + AI systems).We're bootstrapped, profitable, ~100 people, 100% remote US. No PMs telling you what to build — we hire people who take ownership, move fast, and care about craft.The Support Eng role in particular is a rare one: embedded inside our Support function, shipping AI automation and internal tools with a tight feedback loop.All roles are full-time, async-first, US time zones. https://close.com/careers\nApplying here was an odd experience. No acknowledgment or reply even after multiple follow ups. This was from applying back in 2025.\nI've decided to no longer post here after the incredible amount of spam I started receiving, both in terms of direct email submissions as well as unqualified and outright fraudulent applications to my application tracking system.By fraudulent I mean: fake resumes, names stolen from real developers who work at well-known companies but either don't have a linkedin/portfolio or do have a linkedin/portfolio without a profile picture. So easily impersonated by a scammer.It is a real shame, but this thread is now being scraped by plenty of other sites and bad actors.Inbound hiring for remote teams is basically cooked at this point, signal is completely hidden in the noise. Curious if anyone else has had this experience or if it's just me?\nIt happens to candidates! Let's not forget what we have to go through, 6 or 7-stage interview processes, that requires a lot of preparation, as if we don't deserve the time to have a life too. Fake jobs, scammers, dodgy \"take-home tests\" containing malicious packages, cancelled interviews on the day, cancellation of the role in the middle of the hiring process, change of hiring plans, requests to record videos before talking to someone, ghosting, interviewers not interested in interviewing, zero feedback, etc.\nCompanies that have a 7 round interview process are not serious in hiring in general. Sure if some super-genius comes along.But no, it's just a performance. The director can claim they're behind on projects because they don't have enough staff, but everyone they interview isn't qualified (because the interviews are impossible and nearly everyone trips up)I started seeing this pattern recently.The companies that are serious move fast. A chat with the hiring manager. A couple technical interviews, maybe on-site for 2 hours. A chat with someone higher up.  Done, offer made.\nIf you add the initial HR call, that’s 5. The difference between that and the 7 is the chat with CEO and CTO etc. 8 step offer, a no or a low ball. A complete waste of time.\nYep. There was a quote here a few weeks ago, I can't remember from whom now, but the gist of it was that if you have more than a 4-round interview cycle, you're just play acting and being performative, not seriously hiring.\nPlenty of this happening on the other end too. I've received the same exact spam e-mail about an open position from 3 different e-mail addresses / names. It's nuts.On an unrelated note, your localias project is really cool! Going to give it a spin tonight.\nI want to learn more about this.As a job seeker, I see the chaos from my side of the table, I feel like its well known and discussed.The other side of the table however, the recruiters and hiring managers, I want to understand this more. I feel like I could assume the struggles your having, but I would love to see more discussion around this.\nIt is absolutely painful for interviewers and candidates. I used to be able to email managers & founders directly and discuss what they were looking for... today everybody is navigating a deluge of spam and the interview process is becoming dysfunctional.\nIt's not a problem with HN, it's universal at this point. We had a ton of fake candidates like you described come through multiple channels.\nHiring outside your network has always been difficult. A rigorous hiring process should be able to withstand the bad actors. Some people have a good eye for candidates, others do not. Impersonation should be the easiest problem to solve, i.e: if someone is claiming to be someone else based on their LinkedIn profile or website, you can ask that they verify it is theirs. If their profile itself is fraudulent, it will be obvious from their lack of connections and registration date. If you cannot confirm the person is genuine, move on to the next candidate. A good hiring process doesn’t pick people based on where they have worked.\nI have gotten so many fake recruiter contacts, it's not funny. At this point I don't know who is real and who is fake. I talked to real recruiters at Big Tech companies and they said their entire profiles have been fraudulently copied to steal candidate information or to get them to pay to get \"favorable attention\" during the interview process.LinkedIn is doing nothing to stop the fraud at this point. There's almost no way to tell if you're talking to a real person unless you meet with them personally at their office.\n