ack & Backend), Data Engineers, Staff/Lead iOS Engineers, Engineering Managers & Directors, Senior Product Managers | NYC Onsite (4-5 days in-office w/ free catered lunch daily) | https://www.clearme.com/CLEAR is building the secure identity company of the future. Our mission is to make experiences safer and easier—physically and digitally. With more than 38 million Members and a growing network of partners across the world, CLEAR's secure identity platform is transforming the way people live, work, and travel. Whether it’s at the airport, stadium, or throughout your everyday life, CLEAR unlocks the magic of frictionless experiences.If interested, apply here --> https://grnh.se/e4e5dc881us\nHey HN! Air Space Intelligence (https://www.airspace-intelligence.com) is hiring. We are a frontier AI and product company for the critical industries and defense backed by a16z.We’re rebuilding America’s air traffic control system from scratch. What we do in the next two years will define how this country moves through the sky for the next fifty.At the core is one of the largest real-time optimization problems in the world: how do you safely sequence ~40,000 flights/day while routing around weather, military airspace, equipment outages, and constant real-world churn? The system has to be right every time, and reliable at scale.We’re hiring across Backend, Infrastructure, and Frontend (ICs and Tech Leads).One of our roles (with a small puzzle at the bottom that routes to my email): https://www.airspace-intelligence.com/careers/role?=1336c828... - include “HackerNews” in the subject so I can prioritize.If you want a problem that is genuinely hard, consequential, and urgent - this is the moment to reach out.\nFathom – AI Notetaker (fathom.ai)YC W'21, ~100 employees, growing extremely quicklyWe’re the most installed app on HubSpot marketplace and our recent Fathom 3.0 launch was #1 on Product Hunt: https://www.producthunt.com/products/fathomWe’re hiring for both our Full Stack Engineer and AI team.Our team values: Care Deeply, Seek Leverage, Share Ownership, Sustain Urgency, and Be Tenacious.The engineering team works fully remotely (but synchronous), and our AI team is Hybrid (SF based). Multiple team offsites per year.List of all of our open positions (including role descriptions for AI engineering roles and Full Stack Engineer) here: https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/fathom.video* We’re very fast at reviewing applications; yours will be seen within 48 hours of submission! Please indicate that you’re coming from Hacker News.*\nThis is an extremely onerous application process, probably the most so that I've ever seen. While I'm interested in the role, I won't be doing all of that during phase zero before any human has indicated interest in my skills. Just some feedback.\nSigns that it is a seller's market out there. I expect those hiring are being deluged in all sorts of nonsense, and this is one response to it.\nIt's kind of weird that I have to install their app on my computer, but recording a short video isn't that big of a deal, IMO.That said, madiganf: I'd recommend poof-reading that Google Doc in the job posting. There were some malformed sentences. EDIT: Huh, looks like the doc has been edited and the questions themselves have changed a bit. :-)\nSpeakeasy | AI Control Plane | Product, Security and SRE Engineers | SF/London | Full-timeHey everyone! We're staffing up our AI control plane product to meet market demand. Come join a team in San Francisco or London focused on building core infrastructure to help companies securely scale agent use. Think security engineering, observability built on clickhouse, MCP oauth and protocol work, building out our serverless backend and headless experiences. Our team cares deeply about craft and quality and has a track record building highly used developer tools. Team is around 30 and growing!Our technical blog: https://www.speakeasy.com/blogOpen roles: https://www.speakeasy.com/careers#open-rolesor email me 