puter vision algorithms, build Python web services, wrangle large sets of data from disparate classes of sensors, ... any or all, with the only hard requirement being eagerness to learn.Visit covar.com for more information on our current openings!\nForward (getfwd.com) | Austin, TX | ONSITE | Full-timeRebuilding payments for software platforms: transparent economics, no lock-in, hands-on execution. Modern TypeScript stack, real-time streaming, AWS, and heavy investment in agentic AI / LLM orchestration in production.Hiring (all onsite Austin):- Sr Software Engineer (7+ yrs, expert TS full-stack)- Director of Engineering (12+ yrs, scaled 10->50+)- Risk Data Scientist- Incident Management Lead- Risk Intelligence Lead- Founding Growth Marketing Director- Senior Partner Sales ConsultantAll roles + apply: https://www.getfwd.com/careers/Questions: amays+hn@getfwd.com (mention HN)\n500 error when requesting the individual Job Description pages...  ⟫ curl -I https://www.getfwd.com/careers/\nStarbridge | Senior Engineers (Kotlin/Java/React/Typescript) | NYC or Remote | Full-time |[starbridge.ai](https://www.google.com/url?q=http://starbridge.ai&sa=D&sourc...)Starbridge is building an AI platform that turns large-scale public and enterprise data into reliable sales insights. We are early, moving fast, and building from zero to one, so this role will have huge ownership and product impact.Product Engineer: (React/Typescript) who would work closely with product and design to build user-facing parts of the platform. You will craft performant, stable frontends that explain technical concepts to non-technical users and help us iterate fast based on customer feedback.AI Engineer: Applied AI plus strong software engineering. You will build, evaluate, and deploy LLM-driven features like deep document analysis and interactive chat, working with models from OpenAI, Anthropic, and Gemini. Expect hands-on Python, ML system design, experimentation, and production reliability. Bonus for RAG depth and frameworks like LangChain, LlamaIndex, or Hugging Face.Backend Engineer: (looking for Kotlin/Java/Scala experience). You'll work across the backend: building enterprise integrations, large-scale scraping and parsing pipelines, and systems that let users apply LLMs to millions of documents to generate insights at scale.We're looking to build our in-person team in NYC but also open to remote!Apply: [https://starbridge.ai/careers](https://www.google.com/url?q=https://starbridge.ai/careers&s...) and mention HackerNews or email [recruiting@starbridge.ai](mailto:recruiting@starbridge.ai) with your resume.\nI applied on this. My java, react, gcp profile matched perfectly but the recruiter rejected me most possibly due to my stutterring. It felt so bad. I'm capable enough, work US hours, founded a startup, founding engineer twice but couldn't get past recruiter round :(\nGovra | Senior/Staff Full Stack Engineer | Hybrid (SF Bay Area) | Full-timeGovra builds the operating system modern governments run on. We turn dense statutes and tangled rules into executable workflows, embedding intelligence directly into the work so agencies make faster, more accurate and more consistent decisions at scale. We're starting with tax, one of the highest volumes in government, where better decisions mean more revenue, better public services and improved trust between citizens and the state. The result: government that works at the speed of the people it serves.We are seeking a Senior or Staff Software Engineer to help build and scale Govra’s intelligent operating system for governments. You will work closely with the founders, customers and product design teams to ship vital real systems in a fast-moving, high-impact environment. This role is ideal for someone who can go deep technically, think from first principles about product and UX, and move quickly from customer workflows to production code.Apply here: https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4420201620/\nLogenta.ai | Founder/CTO