pending, In-Home Office Setup, Professional Memberships, WFH Meals, Internet Stipend and more! Benefits outside the United States vary by country.\nHiring: Senior Data Engineer ($170-190k), Senior DevOps Engineer ($180-225k), Senior DevOps Engineer - Infrastructure & MLOps ($180-225k), Senior Full Stack AI Engineer - Natural Language Systems ($160-220k), Senior Full Stack AI Engineer - Rapid Prototyping & Analytics ($160-220k), Senior Software Engineer ($170-220k), Support Engineer ($90-125k).Building the AI operating system for healthcare. Join us in applying AI to real-world healthcare workflows where reliability, scale, and user trust matter. Remote US.\nPlanetScale | https://planetscale.com/ | Software Engineer - PlanetScale Postgres | Remote (AMER, LATAM & EMEA) | Base range: $120,000 - $290,000 USDI'm the hiring manager for this position.Come build the best Postgres product on the planet with super talented folks, very high autonomy, tier-zero databases for some of the biggest and fastest growing data sets.Apply at https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/planetscale/jobs/4251150009.Feel free to contact me on LinkedIn or Bluesky if you'd like to talk more about the role. Tell me why Postgres extensions are both great and terrible.\nZūm | Senior/Staff Software Engineer | Hybrid/onsite (Redwood City, CA), Full-timeZūm (ridezum.com) is reinventing K-12 student transportation in the U.S. — a $30B+ industry that moves 26 million kids every school day. Our Connected Mobility Experience (CMX) platform combines modern routing, real-time tracking, and an EV fleet to give school districts a smarter, more transparent alternative to legacy transportation providers. Backed by TPG, Sequoia, and SoftBank with $430M raised at a $1.7B valuation, Zum operates in major districts including San Francisco and Oakland Unified, where they deployed the first all-electric school bus fleet in the country.We're hiring Senior and Staff-level product-oriented backend software engineers as well as 