      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-01-linux-basics-for-hackers-2019",
      "title": "Linux Basics for Hackers (2019)",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/ahegazy0/linux-basics-for-hackers-notes\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48356468\nPoints: 80\n# Comments: 16",
      "body": "Folders and filesNameNameLast commit messageLast commit dateLatest commitHistory5 CommitsLinux.pdfLinux.pdfModule_00_Getting_Started.mdModule_00_Getting_Started.mdModule_01_Terminal_Basics.mdModule_01_Terminal_Basics.mdModule_02_Text_Manipulation.mdModule_02_Text_Manipulation.mdModule_03_Managing_Networks.mdModule_03_Managing_Networks.mdModule_04_Software_Management.mdModule_04_Software_Management.mdModule_05_Permissions.mdModule_05_Permissions.mdModule_06_Process_Management.mdModule_06_Process_Management.mdModule_07_Environment_Variables.mdModule_07_Environment_Variables.mdModule_08_Bash_Scripting.mdModule_08_Bash_Scripting.mdModule_09_Archiving_Compression.mdModule_09_Archiving_Compression.mdModule_10_Filesystem_Storage.mdModule_10_Filesystem_Storage.mdModule_11_Logging_System.mdModule_11_Logging_System.mdModule_12_Using_Abusing_Services.mdModule_12_Using_Abusing_Services.mdModule_13_Security_Anonymity.mdModule_13_Security_Anonymity.mdModule_14_Wireless_Networking.mdModule_14_Wireless_Networking.mdModule_15_Kernel_LKMs.mdModule_15_Kernel_LKMs.mdModule_16_Automation_Jobs.mdModule_16_Automation_Jobs.mdModule_17_Python_Scripting.mdModule_17_Python_Scripting.mdREADME.mdREADME.mdRepository files navigationREADMELinux Basics for Hackers — Course\nA structured course built from personal study notes of the book Linux Basics for Hackers by OccupyTheWeb. Each module breaks down the core concepts, commands, and practical examples in plain English — straightforward enough for beginners, detailed enough to actually be useful.\nLinux Basics For Hackers PDF.\nGetting Started & Setting Up Your Lab\nThe Basics of the Terminal\nThe Kernel & Loadable Kernel Modules\nPlain English explanations of every concept\nAll key commands with examples\nPractice exercises at the end\nVirtualBox or any VM software\nPlaces to practice and go deeper after finishing the modules.\nInteractive Linux lessons in the browser\nLearn Linux by solving security challenges via SSH\nGuided rooms covering Linux basics hands-on\nPractice terminal commands by solving small puzzles\nHack The Box - Linux Fundamentals\nProfessional-level Linux course for security\nThis course is for educational purposes only. Everything here should be practiced in your own lab environment. Never test on systems you don't own or have explicit permission to test.\nLinux Basics for Hackers by OccupyTheWeb — No Starch Press",
